Write a C function that dynamically allocates memory for and initializes several data structures based on user inputs `n` and `m`, representing the sizes of the `items` and `queues` arrays, respectively. The function will create an array of `item` structures, each containing a single `char*` string value, with the number of items determined by `n`. Additionally, it will create an array of `queue` structures, each capable of holding up to `max_size` elements, with the total number of queues determined by `m`. Each `queue` structure will be initialized to be empty at the start.

